# Who has to review a pull request before it can be merged into main.
#
# Pair this with a branch ruleset on `main` that requires a pull request and
# requires review from Code Owners. That combination is what makes "nothing
# lands without my approval" real for other people's contributions.
#
# One thing GitHub does not do: let you approve your own pull request. So this
# file binds contributors, never the maintainer -- who merges their own work
# through the repository-admin bypass, not through self-approval.
